From e1cdddf9d44b8cc2516e6dfc60c8e44d242622d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 09:13:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 043/638] build: use GNU language modes for AROS GCC

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-phase-3

AI_STATUS: complete

ROOT_CAUSE: AROS's GCC cross-toolchain fell through to strict C++20 mode even though Chromium's source uses GNU comma-elision for empty variadic macros.

FIX_REASON: Route AROS through Chromium's existing non-Clang GCC dialect branch instead of rewriting V8 and Chromium macro callsites individually.

SCOPE: build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn

VALIDATION: generated AROS V8 flags use -std=gnu++2a while host V8 remains -std=c++20; target baseline.o passes

RISK: medium; this changes the C/C++ dialect for all AROS target objects, but exactly matches Chromium's documented GCC requirement and preserves the language standard level.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
index 59c46e1b69..3ed383c876 100644
--- a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -641,8 +641,8 @@ config("compiler") {
 
   # C11/C++11 compiler flags setup.
   # ---------------------------
-  if (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android || (is_nacl && is_clang) ||
-      current_os == "aix") {
+  if (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android || is_aros ||
+      (is_nacl && is_clang) || current_os == "aix") {
     if (is_clang) {
       standard_prefix = "c"
 
